<title>JAPAN: Yasuda Trust (Trust Account) reveals problem loans.</title>
<headline>Yasuda Trust (Trust Account) reveals problem loans.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yasuda Trust &amp; Banking Co Ltd has disclosed its restructured loans (in billions of yen unless specified):</p>
<p>					end-Mar 97     end-Mar 96</p>
<p>  Restructured loans	     65.6	    123.9</p>
<p>  Bad loans			  88.2	    104.6</p>
<p>  Non-performing loans	   92.2	    151.5</p>
<p>  Loans to troubled clients    32.4	     48.5</p>
<p>  Total problem loans	   278.4	    428.5</p>
<p>Restructured loans are those on which interest rates have been cut to help corporate restructuring. Bad loans are to bankrupt firms and non-performing are those with interest payments in arrears by six months or more. Loans to troubled clients are mainly to the bank's non-bank affiliates.</p>
</text>
